### 4.3 Enforcing Pinning in CI

Add a CI step that validates no floating ranges exist in `dependencies`:

```bash
# Fail if any production dependency uses ^ or ~
node -e "
const pkg = require('./package.json');
const deps = Object.entries(pkg.dependencies || {});
const floating = deps.filter(([, v]) => /^[\^~]/.test(v));
if (floating.length > 0) {
  console.error('Floating version ranges found in dependencies:', floating);
  process.exit(1);
}
console.log('All production dependencies are pinned to exact versions.');
"
```
